# Corrected 2026-09-01. The previous two digests
#   88f29fd3…  carryover.tsv
#   a72be3cc…  carryover.tsv.gz
# were the retired GENESIS-1 snapshot and did not describe the file in this
# repository. The effect was backwards from a checksum's purpose: a careful
# operator who verified the download would reject a CORRECT carryover.tsv and
# conclude the artifact was tampered with.
#
# The digests above were verified three ways on 2026-09-01:
#   1. sha256 of carryover.tsv.gz in this repo                -> 4d1e2738…
#   2. sha256 of `gunzip -c carryover.tsv.gz`                 -> 84ddbbac…
#   3. sha256 of /home/ubuntu/g4/carryover.tsv on the live
#      archival node 139.180.166.5                            -> 84ddbbac…
# so the file here is byte-identical to the one the live fleet runs.
#
# The node does not rely on this file: it re-checks the carryover against four
# fields committed in mainnet.manifest (file digest, set root, output count,
# total) and refuses to start on any mismatch. This sidecar exists so a
# downloader catches a bad transfer before that point.
